{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement. The parameter `theta` has a built-in prior before it is used in the likelihood. Other data variables (`K`, `N`, `context_idx`, and `sigma`) are context inputs and are not protected.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> K;                       // Number of contexts
  int<lower=0> N;                       // Number of observations
  vector[N] y;                          // Observations
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=K> context_idx; // Context assignments
  real<lower=0> sigma;                  // Measurement variability
}

parameters {
  // Horseshoe parameters
  vector[K] theta;
}

model {
  // Horseshoe prior model
  theta ~ normal(0, 10);

  // Observational model
  y ~ normal(theta[context_idx], sigma);
}

